# Title: Potential Credential Dumping Attempt Using New NetworkProvider - REG
# ID: 0442defa-b4a2-41c9-ae2c-ea7042fc4701
# Status: test
# Level: medium
# Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
# Date: 2022-08-23
# Tags: attack.credential-access, attack.t1003
# Description: Detects when an attacker tries to add a new network provider in order to dump clear text credentials, similar to how the NPPSpy tool does it
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

index=* eventtype=wineventlog (((registry_key_name="*\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\*" AND registry_key_name="*\\NetworkProvider*")) AND NOT ((((registry_key_name="*\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\WebClient\\NetworkProvider*" OR registry_key_name="*\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\LanmanWorkstation\\NetworkProvider*" OR registry_key_name="*\\System\\CurrentControlSet\\Services\\RDPNP\\NetworkProvider*")) OR (process_path="C:\\Windows\\System32\\poqexec.exe"))))
